    <rich_text>Looking for pages within a directory:

First it helps to know which exentsions should be used.
	
	So we fuzz for common used extensions:
			like .html, .aspx, .php using FUZZ in the extension 
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Now that we know which extension we are looking for we can specify our page search even more:
for example for php only:

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <codebox char_offset="193" justification="left" frame_width="1971" frame_height="20" width_in_pixels="1" syntax_highlighting="sh" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0">ffuf -w /opt/useful/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/web-extensions.txt:FUZZ -u http://SERVER_IP:PORT/blog/indexFUZZ</codebox>
    <codebox char_offset="317" justification="left" frame_width="1971" frame_height="20" width_in_pixels="1" syntax_highlighting="sh" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0">ffuf -w /opt/useful/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/directory-list-2.3-small.txt:FUZZ -u http://SERVER_IP:PORT/blog/FUZZ.php&#13;</codebox>
